      "text": "fear him which is able to destroy both soul and body, Matt. 10:28. gain the whole world, and lose his own soul, Matt. 16:26 (Mark 8:36). My soul is exceeding sorrowful, Matt. 26:38 (Mark 14:34). Mary said, My soul doth magnify the Lord, Luke 1:46. this night thy soul shall be required, Luke 12:20 (12:15–21). multitude of them that believed were of one heart and of one soul, Acts 4:32. pray God your whole spirit and soul and body be preserved, 1 Thes. 5:23. dividing asunder of soul and spirit, Heb. 4:12. Which hope we have as an anchor of the soul, Heb. 6:19. they watch for your souls, Heb. 13:17. engrafted word, which is able to save your souls, James 1:21. he which converteth … shall save a soul from death, James 5:20. ye have purified your souls in obeying, 1 Pet. 1:22. fleshly lusts, which war against the soul, 1 Pet. 2:11. I saw under the altar the souls of them that were slain, Rev. 6:9.",
